{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And when Pharaoh saw that the rain had ceased, etc.</b> The meaning is that he did not stand by his declaration in which he said ״HaShem is the righteous one״ etc. even for a brief moment, but immediately and forthwith ״he continued to sin.״ The meaning is that he added to what had come before, for had it been only the first measure it would not have sufficed to hold on to Israel after seeing the marvel of the hail; rather, he added to the boundary of wickedness that was already in him, and he made heavy his heart and the heart of his servants." "<b>Thus concludes the perasha of Va'era.</b>"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:11.351574675Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}